+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Execution kickoff\n\nThe serialized plan review returned a signed PASS at `ae4030bd4a920762e27971f59a7aafdc4fcc0026`. F18 was claimed without an explicit assignee before documentation edits or verification commands.\n\nThe P6 advisory identified the criterion that requires the documentation index and focused user-guide checks to pass. I am retaining that criterion because D1 and D2 already verify the two named checks independently. The conjunction does not merge their evidence or make either result subjective.\n\nThe first review attempt failed before model execution with the remote-tracking ref comparison recorded on `agrologic-oval-bobolink`. A serialized fetch and review completed successfully. The complete error and control result were appended to that bug. No duplicate bug was created.","timestamp":1787528554541713001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Focused RED evidence\n\nBefore editing `docs/user-guide.md`, a focused documentation contract exited 1 at `ae4030bd4a920762e27971f59a7aafdc4fcc0026`. It reported all five expected failures.\n\n- The relation inventory does not include `caused_by`.\n- Mutation guidance contains top-level router extraction detail.\n- Causation guidance contains blame-selection detail.\n- Credential guidance contains the dated incident narrative.\n- Session-log guidance contains pointer-resolution detail.\n\nThe contract reads only the affected guide sections and asserts audience-visible outcomes. It does not enforce punctuation or character choices.","timestamp":1787528622297622001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## GREEN verification evidence\n\nThe focused audience contract that failed before the edit now passes. The relation inventory includes `caused_by`. The selected mutation, causation, credential, and session-log sections no longer contain the implementation or incident details named by the RED contract.\n\nTicket verification passed.\n\n- D1 documentation index and link check passed.\n- D2 passed 19 focused user-guide behavior contracts.\n- D3 documentation vocabulary check passed.\n- D4 `git diff --check` passed.\n\nThe shared documentation generators and guards passed without changing derived files. The documentation-only test lane passed with 3,179 tests and 15 skips. `make lint` passed. `make typecheck` passed across 640 source files. The full test suite was not run because this change modifies only Markdown.\n\n`git diff --name-only` reports only `docs/user-guide.md`. Manual review confirmed that the changed prose follows `docs/documentation-policy.md` without adding any mechanical prose or character check.","timestamp":1787529371359272001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Gerrit review\n\nPushed commit `7fee4acbfa570b834b2bc917ce5febbc3e1b7862` to Gerrit change 2161.\n\nhttps://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2161\n\nThe commit carries `rebar-ticket: a9ec-37db-0d91-483b`, a DCO sign-off, and Change-Id `I0239a06361641223fa40d49e3dcfde784e115eaf`. Local verification and the documentation lane were green before push. The ticket remains in progress pending `LLM-Review +1`, `Verified +1`, and resolution of all review comments.","timestamp":1787529499377014001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Gerrit gates and merge\n\nGitHub Actions run `32675175641` completed successfully in 273 seconds. It produced the following CI evidence.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"run_id\": \"32675175641\",\n  \"status\": \"passed\",\n  \"duration\": 273,\n  \"fixes_applied\": [],\n  \"retry_count\": 0\n}\n```\n\nGerrit change 2161 received `Verified +1` and `LLM-Review +1`. Gerrit reported zero unresolved comments and accepted Submit. The change reached `MERGED` at 2026-08-24 00:05:43 UTC. The GitHub mirror had not advanced when first fetched after submission, so closure remains pending until the merged commit is reachable from `origin/main`.","timestamp":1787529977168864001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787510268565613001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d685b0fb-08ae-43ec-9fb5-ea67877a969e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"70cc-4c1f-b3b9-411d"}],"description":"## Context\n\n`docs/user-guide.md` is the client workflow guide established by handmade-radical-johndory. Its relation inventory omits `caused_by`. Selected sections also explain router extraction, blame-selection internals, a dated credential incident, and session pointer resolution. Those details do not help an audience that uses rebar without developing it.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Add `caused_by` to the client relation inventory with its supported user-facing meaning.\n- Retain observable mutation output, attribution, secret screening, session-log behavior, recovery actions, supported command examples, and safety guidance.\n- Replace router and blame-selection implementation detail with client behavior and links to internal documentation when developers need the mechanism.\n- Replace the credential incident narrative with current recovery guidance and cite coyish-fluent-gibbon only where historical context remains useful.\n- Replace session pointer implementation detail with the behavior a client can rely on.\n- Run the documentation index check and focused user-guide contracts.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The user guide lists `caused_by` with its supported client meaning.\n- [x] Selected workflow sections state observable client behavior without router or blame-selection implementation detail.\n- [x] Credential guidance describes current recovery actions without reproducing the dated incident narrative.\n- [x] Session-log guidance states discoverable behavior without pointer-resolution internals.\n- [x] Existing mutation, attribution, secret-screening, command, and safety guidance remains accurate.\n- [x] Documentation index and focused user-guide checks pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/user-guide.md","reason":"Correct client relation inventory and replace selected implementation and incident narratives with supported behavior."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","b8bf-a5aa-2f4d-44d4"],["relates_to","70cc-4c1f-b3b9-411d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"b8bf-a5aa-2f4d-44d4","parent_status_uuid":"5e26f6a7-bdaa-43e8-8356-ddae499c0a08","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["documentation","accuracy","f18"],"ticket_id":"a9ec-37db-0d91-483b","ticket_type":"task","title":"F18 refocus the user guide on client behavior","verify_commands":[{"command":"python scripts/check_docs_index.py --check","dd_id":"D1","dd_text":"Documentation links and index"},{"command":"python -m pytest tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_caused_by_autoderive_heldout.py tests/interfaces/contracts/test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout.py tests/scripts/test_metrics_docs.py tests/unit/test_user_guide_dc_docs.py -q","dd_id":"D2","dd_text":"User guide behavior contracts"},{"command":"python scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py","dd_id":"D3","dd_text":"Documentation vocabulary gate"},{"command":"git diff --check","dd_id":"D4","dd_text":"Changed file whitespace"}]},"source_event_uuids":["1b7233c3-daf4-4484-b840-7b702ff6a3f2","e02ca83a-5db9-4f7c-a9e7-30716fec6857","bc7046dd-4d6e-4546-ad52-a4375cb69f21","0d63b9d9-26bb-495c-9012-dbeca1dc1d89","4a59fe3d-679a-464a-9385-f6e35ec678f8","c317f628-686e-41a9-bfc7-2410e6d946b2","ae378f55-8b7b-440d-a61d-91d4b88370ff","11255050-85b7-435c-a7e1-bbae6a6582b3","d685b0fb-08ae-43ec-9fb5-ea67877a969e","75fcf46c-2385